# One .env for every app in this repo. Copy to .env at the repo root and fill in. Never commit .env.
# Doctor Dictation finds it by walking up from its package; Count Guard reads count-guard/.env first, then this.
# A variable already set in the shell wins over both files.

# ===== Shared =====
# Ports, so both apps run side by side (`make dev` at the root starts all three).
DD_PORT=8000
CG_API_PORT=8100
CG_WEB_PORT=5173
# One Meta Model API key (https://dev.meta.ai) for the Muse models in both apps:
# Doctor Dictation's Muse STT and LLM_PROVIDER=meta; Count Guard's SAM 3.1, Voice Transcribe and Spark 1.3.
META_API_KEY=

# ===== Doctor Dictation (doctor-dictation/) =====
# Prefer keeping real keys OUT of .env: put them in doctor-dictation/doctor_dictation/secrets.json
# (already gitignored) instead. Precedence per secret: an environment variable
# -- if PRESENT, even when empty -- wins, else doctor_dictation/secrets.json, else "".
# Point to a different secrets file with SECRETS_FILE=/path/to/secrets.json.
# Note: Windows cannot express POSIX 0600 on that file; restrict it with ACLs.
# Example doctor_dictation/secrets.json: {"OPENAI_API_KEY": "sk-...", "DEEPSEEK_API_KEY": "..."}
# Default structuring LLM (prescription JSON): OpenAI. DeepSeek kept as option.
# LLM_PROVIDER=groq uses gpt-oss on Groq (GROQ_API_KEY, GROQ_LLM_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b; -20b is cheaper).
# LLM_PROVIDER=meta uses Muse Spark (META_API_KEY, META_MODEL=muse-spark-1.3, META_BASE_URL).
# Unverified: assumes an OpenAI-style /chat/completions; check before relying on it.
LLM_PROVIDER=openai
LLM_MODEL=gpt-6-luna
# Vision-capable model for the letterhead template tool. Blank reuses LLM_MODEL.
LLM_VISION_MODEL=
OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# OPENAI_API_KEY=   (paste key here; also used for cloud STT default)
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=   (opt-in: uncomment to set via env; prefer doctor_dictation/secrets.json)
DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-chat
DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com
# Deterministic LLM decode: temperature 0 + fixed seed (retried without seed if endpoint rejects it)
DEEPSEEK_SEED=7
# --- STT (cloud-first) ---
# Cloud (OpenAI Whisper API) is the default; the recorded audio is sent to OpenAI
# and is NOT saved by the app. The only STT knobs are STT_ENGINE and WHISPER_MODEL
# (the local fallback model) — there is no in-app model picker.
# STT engine: auto (cloud-first, default) | openai | groq | assemblyai | muse | faster-whisper | onnx (Snapdragon, see doctor_dictation/requirements-onnx.txt)
# groq = Groq hosted Whisper, then local fallback. Needs GROQ_API_KEY (prefer secrets.json).
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_STT_MODEL=whisper-large-v3   (default; whisper-large-v3-turbo is cheaper but makes more word errors)
# assemblyai = AssemblyAI job API (upload + poll, slower), then local fallback. Needs ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY.
# ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY=
# ASSEMBLYAI_MODEL=universal-3-5-pro   (default; universal-2 is cheaper)
# ASSEMBLYAI_MEDICAL=0   (1 = Medical Mode: better drug names, +$0.15/hour)
# muse = Meta Muse Voice Transcribe (needs ffmpeg: audio is converted to WAV), then local fallback.
# META_API_KEY is set once in the Shared section above.
# MUSE_LANGUAGE_BIAS=English   (comma list, e.g. English,Hindi for mixed dictation)
# MUSE_STT_MODEL=muse-voice-transcribe-1.0
STT_ENGINE=auto
# local fallback model ONLY: small.en (default; turbo avoided — too slow on CPU)
WHISPER_MODEL=small.en
WHISPER_DEVICE=cpu
WHISPER_COMPUTE_TYPE=int8
# The dev port is DD_PORT (Shared). PORT is only read by the Docker image (.env.production).

# Largest audio upload /api/transcribe accepts, in bytes (default 10 MiB). Over this -> HTTP 413.
# MAX_AUDIO_BYTES=10485760

# STT chain, tried in order: openai, groq, assemblyai, muse, faster-whisper, onnx, browser. Blank = derived from STT_ENGINE.
# STT_CHAIN=openai,faster-whisper
# Load tests and demos only: lets STT_CHAIN=stub run the fake provider (STUB_TRANSCRIPT, STUB_DELAY_MS).
# ALLOW_STUB_PROVIDERS=1

# --- ACC2 accuracy flags (OFF when unset; production runs both ON; each first save records them in documents.model_versions) ---
# STT_USE_HINTS=1      send the doctor's most-used medicines + common lexicon names as a Whisper vocabulary prompt
# STT_HINT_LIMIT=70    max names in that prompt (~70 fit Whisper's 224-token window)
# STT_TRIM_SILENCE=1   cut long pauses (keeps ~300 ms padding) with ffmpeg before upload; skipped if ffmpeg is missing
# FFMPEG_BIN=ffmpeg    optional path to the ffmpeg binary

# --- Multi-clinic (off by default) ---
# MULTI_CLINIC=1 gives each clinic its own folder under DATA_DIR (directory.db + clinics/<slug>/).
# DB_PATH is ignored in that mode. Create clinics with: python -m doctor_dictation.admin create-clinic --slug rao --name "Rao Clinic"
MULTI_CLINIC=0
# DATA_DIR=/var/lib/doctor-dictation
# Required when MULTI_CLINIC=1: signs session cookies. At least 32 random characters, e.g.
#   python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"
# SESSION_SECRET=
# Local development only: lets the app start without SESSION_SECRET (sessions are then forgeable).
# DEV_INSECURE_SESSION_SECRET=1
# Demo only: lets `python -m doctor_dictation.admin seed-demo` create two FAKE clinics whose doctors have published
# passwords. It refuses a data folder that already has clinics. Never set this outside a demo.
# DEMO_MODE=1

# --- Lexicon promotion (operator only: promote-candidates / promote-apply) ---
# Secret that keys the committed promotion ledger (HMAC), so a rejected name cannot be guessed from its hash.
# Required, 32+ characters; keep it outside git and never reuse a short value (the ledger's 8-hex check value lets
# anyone test guesses offline). Generate with:  python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
# Losing it only means rejected names can be proposed again; a changed pepper is refused against an existing ledger.
# PROMOTION_LEDGER_PEPPER=

# Usernames (comma-separated, case-insensitive) of the app owner, who reviews changes to the shipped medicine and
# investigation lists. Leave empty for no owner: the owner screen then answers 404 to everyone.
# OWNER_USERNAMES=

# ===== Count Guard (count-guard/) =====
# META_API_KEY (Shared) drives SAM 3.1, Voice Transcribe and Spark 1.3. MODEL_API_KEY, if set, wins for Count Guard only.
META_API_BASE=https://api.meta.ai/v1
SAM_MODEL=sam-3.1
VOICE_MODEL=muse-voice-transcribe-1.0
SPARK_MODEL=muse-spark-1.3

# Muse Spark Open on Baseten. The public model id on 15 Oct 2026 was
# meta-models/muse-spark-open. The hackathon spec names the id below.
BASETEN_API_KEY=
SPARK_OPEN_BASE=https://inference.baseten.co/v1
SPARK_OPEN_MODEL=meta-models/muse-spark-open-1026

LOW_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD=0.45
UNANNOUNCED_WINDOW_MS=30000
LOST_AFTER_FRAMES=4
SAM_FPS=2
# COUNT_GUARD_DATA=data
# DECISION_TIER=1   turns the fact card on at start-up (off by default)
